        <h2>Open source</h2>
        <article class="content-card">
          <span class="content-tag">A first milestone · merged</span>
          <h3>My first open-source contribution · CodeTrial</h3>
          <p>I contributed to CodeTrial, an open-source project by NCKU computer science professor Jserv. Its C test harness previously printed non-finite values such as <code>inf</code> and <code>NaN</code> directly into JSON, causing the entire test run to lose its results.</p>
          <p>I added a helper that serializes non-finite <code>double</code> values as JSON <code>null</code>, for both scalar and array outputs, and added regression tests for positive and negative infinity, NaN, and mixed arrays. The fix keeps valid test results available and brings the C harness in line with its C++ and Java counterparts.</p>
          <p>Having my first PR merged felt like a first step from using open-source software to contributing back. It made open collaboration feel more within reach, and encouraged me to keep learning by taking part in public projects.</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/sysprog21/codetrial/pull/441">View merged PR #441 ↗</a> · <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/sysprog21/codetrial/issues/438#issuecomment-6360314135">Issue discussion ↗</a> · <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/sysprog21/codetrial">CodeTrial repository ↗</a></p>
        </article>
      </section>
